  "scope": "Additive source-local Q009 successor that prepares the five logical cases and seven serial stages only in memory as deterministic decks, non-authorizing launch-contract syntax, structurally incomplete policy review candidates, and launch-prohibited restart-continuation handoffs. The trusted-process implementation caches one import-time preparation graph and retains useful exact-comparison and ordinary accidental-drift checks. These in-process checks are explicitly not an authority boundary: privileged same-process CPython can mutate closure cells and code objects and recover mapping-proxy backing dictionaries. Every public result is a source-local review input with no launch, admission, evidence, or publication authority regardless of its contents. The module has no scheduler, live-policy mutation, receipt, admission, persistent-publication, filesystem-write, destructive-cleanup, or CLI surface. Any future authority requires a separately reviewed external process, SHA-256-bound inputs and outputs, receipts, and admission.",
